/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 97 0 R
/T (The Pharmacy Management System \(PMS\) is a centralized relational database platform engineered to streamline and digitize pharmaceutical retail and inventory operations. Modern healthcare management demands seamless trace-ability of drugs, strict adherence to expiration mandates, efficient billing, precise prescription tracking, and robust supplier logistics. Traditional paper-based or file-based management systems lead to data redundancy, stockouts, expired medication risks, and delayed billing customer experiences.)
/E (The Pharmacy Management System \(PMS\) is a centralized relational database platform engineered to streamline and digitize pharmaceutical retail and inventory operations. Modern healthcare management demands seamless trace-ability of drugs, strict adherence to expiration mandates, efficient billing, precise prescription tracking, and robust supplier logistics. Traditional paper-based or file-based management systems lead to data redundancy, stockouts, expired medication risks, and delayed billing customer experiences.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 97 0 R
/T (This mini project delivers a fully normalized relational database schema executed in Structured Query Language \(SQL\). It manages critical domain workflows: inventory categorization, customer prescription compliance, batch tracking, point-of-sale transactions, and supplier replenishment channels. By utilizing strict integrity constraints, transactional ACID properties, automated triggers, and optimized SQL queries, the system ensures data reliability and operational agility for modern healthcare environments.)
/E (This mini project delivers a fully normalized relational database schema executed in Structured Query Language \(SQL\). It manages critical domain workflows: inventory categorization, customer prescription compliance, batch tracking, point-of-sale transactions, and supplier replenishment channels. By utilizing strict integrity constraints, transactional ACID properties, automated triggers, and optimized SQL queries, the system ensures data reliability and operational agility for modern healthcare environments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
